IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-45, TARGETED: the Wage Protection Law, 5718-1958. Draft, target compiler main. No domain expert has read this against the source.
-- THIS ROW DOES NOT ENCODE THE LAW. It records some of the Law's cross-references and some amending instructions as typed values, and tests them.
-- SEAT: the individual to whom the Law is applied, an employee or a former employee. A row of references asks that individual no question: there is no input to ask for, and no @export.
-- NOUNS: the record of one citation (or one amending instruction) and the two questions asked of it. No reference is stated here; they are in wp45-cross-references.l4.
--
-- A citation is encoded as TWO values, as in the cross-reference module of row il-42: what the citing words say they point at, and what the target is in the official text. A test compares them.
-- Two limbs are kept beside them, because a citation can be broken in two ways at once and a reader needs to know which part of the claim was read from what:
--   limb (a): the target is repealed, missing or says something else;
--   limb (b): the citing words still read so in the latest official instrument that touched them.
-- THE KINDS BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's: each is a short plain description I wrote from the citing words and from the target's text, so that two descriptions of the same thing are the same kind.
-- Section numbers are written with Latin letters for the Hebrew ones the Law uses (26C is 26 gimel, 51D is 51 dalet, 19A is 19 alef, 88YA is 88 yod-alef; (a) is alef, (b) bet, (f) vav).

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `What a provision is about` IS ONE OF
    -- P1: a cited law that was repealed
    `the monetary sanction under the Wage Protection (Monetary Sanction) Law, 2009`
    `a repealed law: section 58 of the Law to Increase the Enforcement of Labour Laws, 2011, repeals the Monetary Sanction Law`
    -- P3: a cited category that the Penal Law no longer has
    `farm work done by a prisoner, under subchapter B1 of chapter 6 of the Penal Law`
    `a Penal Law with no farm-work category: its definitions were replaced and section 51D repealed in 2009`
    -- P4: a cited consolidated version that a later one replaced
    `capitalising future payments and benefits in kind, in section 185 of the 1968 Consolidated Version of the National Insurance Law`
    `a 1968 Consolidated Version that the 1995 Consolidated Version replaced, whose section 369 carries the old number 185`
    -- P5: an amending instruction that has not started and will find no words
    `the words naming the postal company, in section 6(a)`
    `the words naming the postal bank and the other listed bodies, in section 6(a)`
    `the words naming the postal company, in section 8(f)`
    `the words naming the postal bank and the other listed bodies, in section 8(f)`
    `the words naming the postal company, in item 8(3) of the Schedule`
    `the words naming the bodies that may hold the account, in item 8(3) of the Schedule`
    -- P6: a cited definition that was deleted
    `the definition of a provident fund in section 47 of the Income Tax Ordinance`
    `a paragraph of the Income Tax Ordinance deleted in 2005, the definition now being in section 1 of the Provident Funds Law`
    -- the sound references kept beside the defects as controls
    `the definition of the subsidiary company of the postal company, in section 88YA of the Postal Law`
    `the limits on paying in cash`
    `the limits on paying by cheque and endorsing a cheque`
    `the fine levels of the Penal Law, by the length of the imprisonment`
    `the entitlement to a benefit when an insolvency order is made against the employer`
    `payments to a fund that stand in place of severance pay when a collective agreement or the Minister of Labour so provides`

DECLARE `How a limb was read` IS ONE OF
    `read from an official instrument`
    `read from an official instrument; the present wording is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
    `CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`

DECLARE `A cross-reference` HAS
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the citing words say it points at` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the target is` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `limb (a) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `limb (b) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (b) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `the instruments and pages read` IS A STRING

DECLARE `A dated commencement` HAS
    `the commencement is in` IS A STRING
    `the day the Hebrew-calendar words name, converted outside L4` IS A DATE
    `the Gregorian date printed beside the Hebrew words` IS A DATE

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the citation points at what it says` MEANS c's `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS c's `the target is`

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs hold` MEANS c's `limb (a) holds` AND c's `limb (b) holds`

GIVEN d IS A `A dated commencement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Hebrew words and the printed date name the same day` MEANS d's `the day the Hebrew-calendar words name, converted outside L4` EQUALS d's `the Gregorian date printed beside the Hebrew words`

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A `How a limb was read`
`how limb (a) was read in` MEANS c's `limb (a) was read`

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A `How a limb was read`
`how limb (b) was read in` MEANS c's `limb (b) was read`
